      "writtenOn": "2019-08-16T17:56:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The fsm is only getting reset when SDA is stuck at 0.\nIf SDA is stuck at 1 (i2cs is in the middle of a read and outputting a 0), we are relying on the next transaction to reset the fsm.\nI think there may be a small chance that a stuck at 1 may turn into a stuck at 0 after the transaction, but this requires a lot of events to line up (such as the read acks).\nBut this scenario is rare, so it may not be worth preventing?",
      "parentUuid": "3315d3b2_880690ec",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 139,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 140,
        "endChar": 28
      },
